id: hac-of5a
title: Add agent-native automation trace diagnostics
description: Expose the stable Home Assistant automation and script trace contracts through typed bounded CLI commands for execution diagnosis and agent workflows.
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 0
tags[7]: agents,automation,diagnostics,home-assistant,script,trace,websocket
created_at: "2026-08-07T16:44:25.127Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T16:44:25.127Z"
deadline: "2026-08-08T16:44:25.127Z"
assignee: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: Typed hassio ws traces list get and contexts commands validate automation and script domains before network I/O; List and context output is deterministic bounded countable and available in all six supported formats while exact get preserves the Core payload; Detailed nested help machine schema capability probes README and every relevant docs page stay synchronized; Built and installed hassio commands pass local Core live read-only acceptance without persisting private values; Build typecheck lint docstrings duplication file-size ShellCheck audit Trivy PM changelog auto-release dry-run package smoke and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage gates pass
definition_of_ready: Official Core 2026.8.0 contracts inspected; local Core 2026.7.4 capability proven; all-status PM searches and duplicate scan found no existing trace item; repository is clean on a dedicated branch.
goal: agent-native-home-assistant-operations
objective: typed-runtime-diagnostics
value: Let operators and LLM agents explain why automations and scripts ran failed or stopped without manually composing WebSocket payloads.
impact: Faster incident diagnosis with token-bounded machine-readable evidence and safer read-only defaults.
outcome: Current and backward-compatible trace discovery and retrieval with complete production evidence.
why_now: Core 2026.8.0 confirms stable trace contracts and the CLI just completed typed automation runtime execution but lacks the corresponding diagnosis path.
